{"kind": "mod", "id": 1232, "name": "Lotus", "slug": "lotus", "teaser": "Custom Trader with over 340+ Quests, 900+ sold and bartered items and a special keycard that gives infinite labs access.", "owner_name": "Lunnayaluna", "downloads": 179320, "favourites": 102, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": true, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "com.luna.lunnayalunalotus", "thumbnail_local": null, "category": "Quests", "category_id": 7, "updated_at": "2026-08-01T12:19:20.000000Z", "created_at": "2024-01-17T20:08:28.000000Z", "published_at": "2026-04-11T19:39:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.0.2", "latest_version": "1.7.3", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p><strong>Lotus’ first Quest should show up at Player Level 5</strong></p>\n<p>Don’t forget to make backups of your profile when adding / removing / updating any mods. Also check out all the different info tabs and read the pinned comment if you wanna report any bugs or issues to me**</p>\n<p>**Please check the “Installation” tab to see how to install Lotus properly</p>\n<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Features</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Features</strong></p>\n<p><strong>“Lotus” currently features the following things :</strong></p>\n<p>- 340+ Custom Quests</p>\n<p>- 900+ Sold / Bartered Items, including a lot of Items that are not available on traders, good ammo and good armor plates</p>\n<p>- A Custom Keycard that grants you infinite Labs access for free, unlocked by Quests</p>\n<p>- A very cute face</p>\n<p><strong>You might not be able to finish all Quests in a single playthrough unless you use Profile Editor to unlock the failed Questlines</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This is not the final version of the mod, with all the updates I try my best to adjust Lotus to be up to date with new content, quests, balancing, etc.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>See “Planned Features” tab for future plans</strong></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Installation ( Please Read )</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Installation</strong></p>\n<p>Step 1.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Download <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1717-lotus/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Lotus</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Download <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2310/wtt-commonlib\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">WTT-commonlib</a> if you are on 4.0.x,\nif you are on 3.11.x or lower, download <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/885-virtual-s-custom-quest-loader/?highlight=virtua#overview\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Virtual’s Custom Quest Loader</a> instead</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Step 2.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unzip the files ( <em>preferably with 7zip</em> )</li>\n<li>Drag the “BepInEx” and “user” folders from the Lotus and VCQL zip files directly into your SPT install ( <em>like most other mods</em> )</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Step 3.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Start your game and have fun</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>You should use 7zip and should avoid using some form of mod-installer / mod-manager to prevent possible issues</strong></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-3\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Known Issues</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Known Issues</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Conflicts with certain settings in <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/379-server-value-modifier-svm/?highlight=serv\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Server Value Modifier [SVM]</a>, those would be :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enabling “Remove Filters” for the following cases ( <em>Case Space Manager</em> )<br />\n- WZ Wallet<br />\n- Wallet<br />\n- S I C C Case<br />\n- Documents Case<br />\n- Keycard Holder</li>\n<li>Enabling “Remove key-card requirement to access laboratory” ( <em>Raid Settings</em> )</li>\n<li>Enabling “Unlock trader offers behind quests” ( <em>Traders</em> )</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Conflicts with Lotus’ Weapon-Assembly Tasks :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Enabling the Attachment changes in <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/606-spt-realism-mod/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SPT Realism Mod</a> will likely make all of Lotus’ gunsmith tasks not work at all</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1033-kalashnikov-enhanced-modding/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Kalashnikov Enhanced Modding</a> <em>might</em> make the AK-builds from the solutions not have the correct stats or work at all, the quests will likely still be possible to complete</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Too many mods that add traders are installed and Lotus can’t be accessed anymore :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Solution A would be installing <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1508-kaeno-traderscrolling/?highlight=traders\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Kaeno-TraderScrolling</a></li>\n<li>Solution B would be enabling the “Trading Intermediate Screen” in the default Tarkov ingame settings</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>BTR Driver having a messed up dialog screen :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Being able to start more than 1 BTR quest at a time mixes up all the dialog options, from my experience this shouldn’t break anything, just ruins the immersion</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Modded Weapons / Gear not working for quests :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sadly how EFT quests work, modded items have different IDs and don’t count towards these quests by default, I might make some sort of compatibility / config for that in the future but it would be a ton of work</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-4\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Future Plans</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Future Plans</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Always expanding existing questlines</li>\n<li>Fully rework all the questlocks</li>\n<li>Fully rework the quest order and Lotus’ progression in general</li>\n<li>Making certain quests / questlines matter more for the story so they aren’t just simple “sidequests” that unlock a few new items</li>\n<li>Making more story-related questlines involving other traders</li>\n<li>Involving all vanilla traders into the storyline ( <em>so far only ref and lightkeeper are left</em> )</li>\n<li>A custom model for Lotus’ Keycard</li>\n<li>Creating custom quest items that spawn in scripted locations</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-5\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Recommended Mods</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Recommended Mods</strong></p>\n<p><strong>All of these mods are pretty much fully compatible with Lotus from my experience</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please make sure to read their respective modpages and check for dependencies, thank you</strong></p>\n<p><strong>A list of mods that are overall very good and pair very well with Lotus (</strong> <em>in no particular order</em> <strong>) :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1860-ui-fixes/?highlight=ui%20f\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">UI Fixes</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1114-task-list-fixes/?highlight=task\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Task List Fixes</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2853-expanded-task-text-ett/?highlight=task\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Expanded Task Text (ETT)</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1814-modding-stats-helper-by-wara/?highlight=wara\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Modding Stats Helper - by wara</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1795-trader-modding-and-improved-weapon-building/?highlight=trader\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Trader Modding And Improved Weapon Building</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1981-dynamic-maps/?highlight=dynamic\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Dynamic Maps</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/652-game-panel-hud/?highlight=game\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Game Panel HUD</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2117-trader-qol/?highlight=trader%20q\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Trader QoL</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2922-p-a-i-n-painstaking-agony-induced-nuisance/?highlight=pain\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">P.A.I.N. - Painstaking Agony Induced Nuisance</a></li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/379-server-value-modifier-svm/?highlight=server\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Server Value Modifier [SVM]</a> Check the “Known Issues” tab to see what settings not to use when using SVM with Lotus</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Mods that are highly recommended to use with Lotus :</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1508-kaeno-traderscrolling/?highlight=trader\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Kaeno-TraderScrolling</a> A must have when using multiple additional traders</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1861-skipper/?highlight=skipp\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Skipper</a> Incase something is wrong with a quest or you don’t want to complete them</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1159-morecheckmarks/?highlight=more\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MoreCheckmarks</a> With the amount of quests that Lotus comes with, this is basically a must have</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2462-flea-limiter/?highlight=flea%20l\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Flea Limiter</a> Since Lotus’ is intended to be played without the flea market or a limited flea market, and is balanced around that, but with anything else here, the choice is up to you</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2108-ref-spt-friendly-quests/?highlight=ref\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Ref - SPT Friendly Quests</a> for a better experience with the ref quests</li>\n<li><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2109-bosses-have-lega-medals/?highlight=bosses\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bosses Have Lega Medals</a> Lotus also adds items to ref ( <em>since 1.6.0</em> ) this might help with obtaining some lega medals</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Make sure mods that apply changes to custom quests load after <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/885-virtual-s-custom-quest-loader/?highlight=quest%20l\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Virtual’s Custom Quest Loader</a> and after certain Trader mods if you want to apply these changes to the traders themselves, I suggest using <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1082-loe-load-order-editor/?highlight=load\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">LOE (Load Order Editor)</a> to change your load order</strong></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-6\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Quest Guide</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Quest Guide</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Lotus has a ton of quests and that means that I cant give a detailed guide for each of them, if you’re struggling with finding certain places, I really recommend one of these mods ( <em>or both</em> ) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&gt;&gt; <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/1981-dynamic-maps/?highlight=dynamic\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Dynamic Maps</a> &lt;&lt;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&gt;&gt; <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/652-game-panel-hud/?highlight=game\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Game Panel HUD</a> &lt;&lt;</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Lotus has some Quests that tell you to do something while wearing “specified Gear”, what is this gear and how do I know what is required?</strong></p>\n<p>That is simple, I made sure to drop as much information as possible in the description, you will need to scroll down to see it for some Quests however.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/9hj53ni.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9hj53ni.png\" alt=\"9hj53ni.png\" /></a></p>\n<p>The “specified Gear” for this Quest:</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/mmqxrhl.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/mmqxrhl.png\" alt=\"mmqxrhl.png\" /></a></p>\n<p>The purpose of this is to give more information since some quests give you multiple options for gear, and to have a shorter objective length,</p>\n<p>so it does not look like this abomination ( Test Drive - Part 1 )</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/ex0sklN.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ex0sklN.png\" alt=\"ex0sklN.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><strong>There are a lot of Quests where I need to find and handover items, how do I know what actually needs to be “found in raid”?</strong></p>\n<p>Very simple again, the objectives always tell you if something needs to be found in raid or not.</p>\n<p>If it only tells you to “Obtain xyz” and / or just “Hand over xyz” without mentioning anything about “in raid”,</p>\n<p>it doesnt need to be FiR.</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/Vd0X99C.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Vd0X99C.png\" alt=\"Vd0X99C.png\" /></a></p>\n<p>If a quest needs items found in raid, it usually tells you that in the objective like “Find xyz in raid” and then “Hand over xyz”</p>\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://i.imgur.com/e9ABa8s.png\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/e9ABa8s.png\" alt=\"e9ABa8s.png\" /></a></p>\n<p><strong>There are a few questlines where you need to choose a specific trader for the questline that you want</strong></p>\n<p>The 2 big questlines that you can pick are for either Prapor or Peacekeeper / Skier.</p>\n<p>You can choose the questline you want after accepting the quest “<em><strong>For The Motherland</strong></em>” from Prapor, after accepting it you should get a quest from Peacekeeper called “<em><strong>Keeping The Peace</strong></em>”.</p>\n<p><strong>&gt; Completing the quest from Peacekeeper will get you his questline with 16 Quests ( 13 from PK and 3 from Skier )</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&gt; Completing the quest from Prapor will get you his questline with 17 Quests</strong></p>\n<p>Then there are a few smaller quests, you will get a quest called “<strong>New Dealer In Town</strong>” from Lotus. Accepting it will give you a quest from Skier, completing the quest for their respective trader will give you another quest for the trader that you picked.</p>\n<p>The objectives of the quests that you will get after are identical, with the only difference being the rewards and the trader they are on.</p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-7\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">“I dont like the Trader Icon”</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Changing the trader image</strong></p>\n<p>Don’t like the trader icon or the style?</p>\n<p>That’s completely fine, you can change it to whatever you like by using certain mods.\nYou can also find the image under: SPT/user/mods/Lotus/res</p>\n<p><strong>Make sure your own image is a .jpg !</strong></p>\n<p>I use this mod for all the traders I have for example :</p>\n<p>&gt;&gt;&gt; <strong><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://hub.sp-tarkov.com/files/file/2113-merks-trader-image-switcher/?highlight=trader%20image\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">MERKS TRADER IMAGE SWITCHER</a> &lt;&lt;&lt;</strong></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-8\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Lotus Assort</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Lotus Assort ( <em>v.1.4.2</em> )</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Here are a few examples of what Lotus can sell ( <em>if all of the quests are completed</em> ) :</strong></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ko2e7bZ.png\" alt=\"ko2e7bZ.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/nRKxpxS.png\" alt=\"nRKxpxS.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pBj689n.png\" alt=\"pBj689n.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/BpfT6GU.png\" alt=\"BpfT6GU.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/PB89L25.png\" alt=\"PB89L25.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Y9IeIni.png\" alt=\"Y9IeIni.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZlPzpTg.png\" alt=\"ZlPzpTg.png\" /></p>\n<p><strong>The images don’t include every item that Lotus sells, also about half of the items in Lotus’ assort are <em>locked</em> behind quests, some easier and some more difficult to help with balancing.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Armored Vests / Rigs are sold <em>without</em> any plates, this is not a bug nor an issue - this is <em>intented</em> to let the user buy any armor and then seperately buy any plates of their choice, have fun!</strong></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-9\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Weapon Assembly Task Solutions</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Weapon Assembly Task Solutions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The shown builds are for 3.11.x and 4.0.x , builds for 3.10.x can be found in the Lotus thread in the official SPT discord server :</strong></p>\n<p><strong><a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.com/channels/875684761291599922/1234841569035812904/1370342379416064091\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https://discord.com/channels/875684761291599922/1234841569035812904/1370342379416064091</a></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Important Note: The Insight WMX200 Tactical Flashlight is not actually considered a “standalone flashlight” but a tactical device, so it won’t work for quests that require a normal flashlight, this is a Tarkov issue</strong></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/DQZi6WL.png\" alt=\"DQZi6WL.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/CdiQuBn.png\" alt=\"CdiQuBn.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/dXexODZ.png\" alt=\"dXexODZ.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/fbMyVJS.png\" alt=\"fbMyVJS.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/uoctHdL.png\" alt=\"uoctHdL.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/aJYuCmK.png\" alt=\"aJYuCmK.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9yCHPkO.png\" alt=\"9yCHPkO.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/LnLDpxF.png\" alt=\"LnLDpxF.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/z0s7xb2.jpeg\" alt=\"z0s7xb2.jpeg\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/lsnV0L4.png\" alt=\"lsnV0L4.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/mamDbXP.png\" alt=\"mamDbXP.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/GDt9Nbh.png\" alt=\"GDt9Nbh.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Dd3YCuL.png\" alt=\"Dd3YCuL.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/cs4qp99.png\" alt=\"cs4qp99.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TpDsbva.jpeg\" alt=\"TpDsbva.jpeg\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/4Rz3gN1.png\" alt=\"4Rz3gN1.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/OLrKuO1.png\" alt=\"OLrKuO1.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/20flSpT.png\" alt=\"20flSpT.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/UUtSE7R.png\" alt=\"UUtSE7R.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/C9Kji3h.png\" alt=\"C9Kji3h.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/F7F2wqu.png\" alt=\"F7F2wqu.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TLj2pKf.png\" alt=\"TLj2pKf.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vOa0jg0.png\" alt=\"vOa0jg0.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/QvLxFmI.png\" alt=\"QvLxFmI.png\" /></p>\n<p><img loading=